# OpenShore app build-time env. Copy to .env.local and fill in. Everything here is
# OPTIONAL: with all of it blank, OpenShore runs local-first with no accounts and
# no billing, exactly as before. Only VITE_-prefixed vars reach the client, and
# only public values ever belong here (never a service-role or secret key).

# --- Sign-in (Supabase) ---
# From the Supabase project: Settings -> API. The anon key is public by design.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Billing (Stripe) ---
# The publishable key is safe to ship. Seats are purchased on the web
# (openshore.ai/os-code), never inside the iOS app (Apple 3.1.1).
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Google Drive (gitOS storage provider) ---
# From the Google Cloud project: APIs & Services -> Credentials. Two OAuth
# clients are required by Google's own native-app rules, not a choice: an
# "iOS" client (bundle id ai.openshore.oscode) for the phone, and a
# "Desktop app" client for Electron. Neither secret is confidential for a
# PKCE public client (RFC 8252); the desktop secret Google still issues is
# required by its token endpoint, so it ships here as a build constant,
# never through the device secret store, because it is not per-user data.
VITE_GDRIVE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GDRIVE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GDRIVE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Repositories: one-tap OAuth (GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket) ---
# Only the PUBLIC client id belongs here. The matching client SECRETs live in
# the repo-oauth edge function (set with `supabase secrets set`), never in this
# client build. This is the GitHub App path Claude Code uses: the secret half of
# the handshake runs on the server. With a client id blank, that provider simply
# keeps the paste-a-token path. Register:
#   GitHub  -> a GitHub App, https://github.com/settings/apps  (client id Iv...)
#   GitLab  -> an Application, https://gitlab.com/-/user_settings/applications
#   Bitbucket -> an OAuth consumer, workspace settings -> OAuth consumers
# The single redirect URI to register on all three:
#   <VITE_SUPABASE_URL>/functions/v1/repo-oauth/callback
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GITLAB_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_BITBUCKET_CLIENT_ID=
